
# <type>(<scope>): <summary>      imperative, lower-case, no full stop, <= 72 chars
#
# type:  feat | fix | eval | test | docs | refactor | chore
# scope: deid | extract | mcp | viewer | eval | data | docs | config   (optional)
#
# Body (optional, wrap at 72): what changed and why, not how.
# Include numbers when they changed, e.g. "dev leak recall 0.81 -> 0.96".
#
# Examples:
#   feat(deid): add NRIC/FIN recogniser with checksum
#   fix(extract): reject evidence spans that cross a surrogate tag
#   eval(deid): score pattern-only recall on dev
#   docs: add architecture diagram to README
#   chore(config): add requirements.txt and .env.example
#
# Never commit .env, vault/, runs/ or anything from the test split's outputs.
